  "note": "ADVISORY, and it decides WHICH shard a spec runs in, never WHETHER: a file absent from this map is still discovered by 'playwright test --list' and packed as the HEAVIEST file in the suite, so staleness costs balance and never coverage (docs/BACKLOG.md GATE-1). BUT the number of such guesses is now GATED: 'e2e complete' runs --check-manifest and refuses when more than MAX_GUESSED_SHARE (10 %) of the packed weight is unmeasured, printing the missing entries calibrated from that run. Re-measured IN FULL 2026-09-23 after 36360ae's shard 4 hit its 40-minute step timeout with 0 failures: 31 of 175 files were unmeasured (65 % of the packed weight guessed) and the older entries had moved unevenly (1.3x-5.3x, median 2.2x), so a merge onto the 2026-08-29 numbers was not enough. One serial single-worker run of all 176 files on a 4-core dev container UNDER LOAD (1-min load 6-16 from other agents; 9 of 885 tests failed as contention flakes and their seconds are kept), so absolute seconds are ~1.8x a CI runner's; only the RATIOS between files matter to the packer. Five specs that landed during the run were added with --merge, calibrated at 1.01x over 5 files re-run alongside them. 2026-09-24, after d0604c5's shard 4 timed out again (steps 32.0 / 28.8 / 33.9 / 40.0 min): pick-proxy-collision added, and 16 entries re-entered with --merge --update - the edited specs (camera-restore included) plus pick-mark-seat, gauge-hooks and pick-anchor, which 9404cb1's seat-stamp change (3 confirm frames per settle) moved up ~1.3x against the non-pick ruler. Ruler: 7 unedited non-pick files (0.62x), then 4 (0.53x, a quieter box) for pick-proxy-collision and camera-restore. Checked against CI: this manifest predicts d0604c5's four shards at 33.8 / 29.7 / 32.5 / 38.8 min (rms 2.4) where the 09-23 one gave rms 5.9 (pick-proxy-collision, then unmeasured, counted as 0). Other seat-heavy specs were NOT re-measured and are probably ~1.3x light, the residual in that fit. Refresh: ALL shards of ONE run with --emit-durations, or new files only with --emit-durations REPORT --merge (runs >= 3 already-measured specs alongside them for the calibration). REBALANCED 2026-10-22 against 7479bde's six CI shards (test steps 35.7 / 23.0 / 34.9 / 24.5 / >33, cancelled, taken as 35.7 / 33.9 min, all green): each measured file was multiplied by its shard's CI-to-planned ratio over the run-wide 0.594, i.e. 1.14 / 0.94 / 1.12 / 0.78 / 1.14 / 1.08, so the manifest keeps its scale and only the balance moved. Shard 2's ratio prices the unmeasured roof-member-renumber at 2 tests x the median 15.3 s/test; the file itself stays unmeasured. A per-shard ratio cannot tell which file in a shard moved, so the next full --emit-durations replaces this.",
